
Option: -o <value> | --option=<value>

Option to create the output file using the specified options or input option file. 

quartus_pfg -c -o <parameter=value> --option <parameter=value> <input file> <output file> [secondary output file(s)]
quartus_pfg -c -o option.txt <input file> <output file> [secondary output file(s)]
    
You can create an option file using any text editor. Use the following format to specify parameter values
in option file:

<parameter>=<value>
    
Use "quartus_pfg -l" or "quartus_pfg --list" to list the valid parameters and values for the options.
    
Example:
quartus_pfg -c -o device=EPCQL1024 -o flash_loader=1SX280LU3S1 -o bitswap=ON test.sof test.jic test.map test.rpd        

